[6.1638, "o", "Molecule + Podman + systemd pre-flight check\r\n"]
[6.1649, "o", "host: Linux x86_64\r\n\r\n== 1. Control groups (cgroups)\r\n"]
[6.1658, "o", "  PASS  cgroup v2 is in use (cgroup2fs)\r\n"]
[6.1665, "o", "\r\n== 2. Podman (the container engine)\r\n"]
[6.1816, "o", "  PASS  podman found: podman version 5.8.7\r\n"]
[6.1833, "o", "        major version 5 is supported\r\n"]
[6.2726, "o", "  PASS  podman runs rootless (recommended)\r\n\r\n== 3. Rootless user-id mapping (newuidmap / subuid / subgid)\r\n"]
[6.2733, "o", "  PASS  newuidmap found: /usr/bin/newuidmap\r\n"]
[6.275, "o", "  PASS  /etc/subuid has an entry for youruser\r\n"]
[6.2761, "o", "  PASS  /etc/subgid has an entry for youruser\r\n"]
[6.2766, "o", "\r\n== 4. SELinux (Linux only)\r\n"]
[6.2779, "o", "  PASS  SELinux is Enforcing - this is the well-tested case\r\n"]
[6.2784, "o", "        You do NOT need: setsebool container_manage_cgroup, /etc/containers/policy.json edits,\r\n        or --security-opt label=disable. Podman labels systemd containers container_init_t.\r\n\r\n== 5. Python (Molecule needs Python 3.10 or newer)\r\n"]
[6.2886, "o", "  PASS  python3 found: 3.14\r\n"]
[6.2894, "o", "  PASS  python3 is new enough (need >= 3.10)\r\n\r\n== 6. Molecule and the Podman driver\r\n"]
[7.1006, "o", "  PASS  molecule \u001b[32m26.9.0\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.321, "o", "  PASS  the 'podman' driver is available (from molecule-plugins)\r\n\r\n== 7. The containers.podman Ansible collection\r\n"]
[7.6219, "o", "  WARN  containers.podman is not installed yet\r\n        You do not need it installed up front. 'molecule test' installs it from\r\n        requirements.yml during the 'dependency' step. Run 'ansible-galaxy collection\r\n        install containers.podman' if you want it now.\r\n"]
[7.6229, "o", "\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nRESULT: READY WITH WARNINGS - 1 warning(s), no hard failures\r\nYou can continue. Read each WARN line before you start.\r\n"]
